<title>INDIA: Indian forex reserves rise to $22.41 bln on Aug 23.</title>
<headline>Indian forex reserves rise to $22.41 bln on Aug 23.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $22.41 billion on August 23, 1996, from $22.36 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>	 FOREIGN EXCHANGE RESERVES (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					   Aug 23     Aug 16	 Aug 25</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     17,985	17,887	 18,994</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,410	  4,445</p>
<p>    SDRs				    19	    61	     46</p>
<p>    Total			     22,414	22,358	 23,485</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
